ts every LLMError uniformly as a non-success, without stating a disposition word per arm — so a retryable Bedrock throttle (429 / WAIT_AND_RETRY / exit-11) and a permanent auth/config failure both collapse to the same plain non-zero exit, masking the retryable disposition.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc15a3eac5409db69","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan bullet: 'Have the live selected-criteria loop return a success count so --require-live can fail when live execution was attempted but produced zero successful evaluations.'","norm_id":"n79b5d61c530e789c","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A Bedrock 429 throttle under --require-live surfaces the same non-zero exit as a permanent credential error, so a retryable condition is reported as a hard failure instead of exit-11/WAIT_AND_RETRY.","The newly-allowed 'attempt live even when uncredentialed' Bedrock path fails on missing creds and, under --require-live, is indistinguishable from a genuine eval regression."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"When the live loop yields zero successes under --require-live, distinguish transient LLMError (via classify_llm_failure) from permanent failures and preserve the most-recoverable disposition — e.g. exit-11/WAIT_AND_RETRY on a retryable throttle, plain non-zero only on fatal/config failures.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"insufficient","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"l